Subject: [PATCH] wayland: transfer keyboard focus state without replaying presses

Based on Gamescope 3.16.28 (fa0b4d3342078f01eadff0193e09c3b561f40c03).

A key that dismisses another application can still be held when Gamescope
receives keyboard focus. Sending it through HandleKey creates a second
press in the nested client. Preserve the host keymap, keys and modifiers
through the seat's leave/enter path instead, and pair shortcut releases
with the presses actually handled by that shortcut.

Regression check: python3 check-focus.py PATH_TO_PATCHED_GAMESCOPE_SOURCE
See README.md for scope and remaining end-to-end validation.

